   $q$Which choice expresses a complete thought with a subject and a main verb?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Since whoever finishes the trail survey first enters the data into the shared spreadsheet.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"subordinate-clause-fragment"},{"text":"The student who finishes the trail survey first, entering the data into the shared spreadsheet.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"participle-fragment"},{"text":"Whoever finishes the trail survey first will enter the data into the shared spreadsheet.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Whoever finishes the trail survey first and enters the data into the shared spreadsheet.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"noun-clause-fragment"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Whoever finishes the trail survey first will enter the data into the shared spreadsheet.$q$, $q$The noun clause "Whoever finishes the trail survey first" is the subject, and "will enter" is the main verb. In the choice with "and enters," both verbs belong inside the noun clause, so the sentence has a subject but no main verb.$q$, 'draft', null)
