   $q$Read the sentence: "The glued pages dried under heavy weights overnight, then the bookbinder trimmed the edges." Which revision fixes the error?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The glued pages dried under heavy weights overnight, and then the bookbinder trimmed the edges.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The glued pages dried under heavy weights overnight. Then the bookbinder trimming the edges.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fragment-created"},{"text":"The glued pages dried under heavy weights overnight, then, the bookbinder trimmed the edges.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-unfixed"},{"text":"The glued pages dried under heavy weights overnight then the bookbinder trimmed the edges.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fused-sentence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The glued pages dried under heavy weights overnight, and then the bookbinder trimmed the edges.$q$, $q$"Then" is an adverb, not a coordinating conjunction, so the original is a comma splice; adding "and" correctly joins the clauses. Putting a comma after "then" does not change the fact that two independent clauses are joined only by commas.$q$, 'draft', null)
