-- Passage wg12-writing-with-evidence-p06
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('c1b0f55b-26fe-5cb1-a767-e8fc11297af6', 'wg12-writing-with-evidence-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g12-writing-with-evidence'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Draft: Lights on Mercer Street$q$, $q$(1) Urban planner Yusra Bakr's report "After Dark on Mercer Street" examines a weekly night market that the town of Elmhurst Falls began hosting in 2019. (2) Every Friday from May to September, the town closes four blocks to cars, and local cooks, artists and farmers set up stalls under strings of lights. (3) Bakr argues that the market's most important effect was not the sales at the stalls but the change in how residents thought about the street after dark. (4) Before the market, Bakr notes, most of the street's shops closed by six o'clock, and residents described Mercer Street in surveys as "empty" and "forgotten." (5) ____, by 2022 eleven shops had extended their hours to nine o'clock on every weeknight, not just on market nights.

(6) This detail is the strongest support for Bakr's claim. (7) If the market helped only the stall owners, the shops would have no reason to stay open on Tuesdays and Wednesdays. (8) Bakr also reports that the number of empty storefronts fell from fourteen to five over the same period. (9) My cousin went to the market last summer and bought a painted clay bowl. (10) Bakr admits that a new apartment building opened two blocks away in 2021, which may have brought in more customers. (11) However, the shops began extending their hours in 2020, a full year before the apartments opened, which suggests the market started the change.

(12) Overall, night markets are fun events that every town should try.$q$, 'draft')
